// Raw DEFLATE, RFC 1951:
// https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1951
//
// The three block types and the two code tables, both directions, shaped for a
// stream that outlives one message. Compression chooses the block type per
// message — dynamic codes for the symbols it actually uses, the fixed code when a
// header would cost more than it saves, stored for octets that do not repeat — with
// a window the caller sets and, optionally, a window that survives a message
// boundary; decompression reads blocks until the octets run out at a block
// boundary, may reach back into the messages before it, and stops at a ceiling.
//
// This exists because permessage-deflate needs a DEFLATE stream it can stop and
// resume inside (RFC 7692 §7.2), which is a shape a file compressor does not
// have to offer.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moonhttp/deflate",
  "moonbitstack/moonzip/deflate" @zip,
} for "test"

import {
  "moonbitstack/moonzip/deflate" @zip,
} for "wbtest"
